  "content": {
    "id": "v2-dd963-p17-practice-slot-7-lower-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve $\\sin x(2\\cos x-\\sqrt3)=0$ for $x\\in[0,2\\pi)$. Answer in exact form if possible, otherwise round to 3 d.p.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=0,\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\pi,\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$",
      "worked": "$\\sin x=0$ or $2\\cos x-\\sqrt3=0$.\n\nFor $\\sin x=0$, $x=0,\\pi$ on the given domain.\n\nFor the second factor:\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\cos x&=\\sqrt3\\\\\\cos x&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{6}.\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is positive in Q1 and Q4, so $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$.\n\nTherefore $x=0,\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\pi,\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
